---
import Mark from '../brand/Mark.astro';
import PlainSummary from '../PlainSummary.astro';
---
<section class="sec" id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-h" data-depth="0.2">
  <div class="tube tube--side" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow">INCIDENT REPORT · READING CONDITIONS</p>
      <h2 class="h2 recede-h" id="problem-h">The archive was built to edit, not to read.</h2>
      <p class="narr recede">The SCP Wiki is one of the internet’s great collaborative works: thousands of writers, nearly twenty thousand files, decades of dread. Its reading conditions are, per standing assessment, poor. Cramped columns, tiny text, no dark mode worth the name, no offline access, and it forgets you the moment you close the tab. Personnel have been studying hazardous material in bad light. Deepwell fixes the reading and leaves the archive exactly where it belongs: free, open, and credited to the people who wrote it.</p>
      <PlainSummary>The wiki is great to read and hard on the eyes. Deepwell is a better way to read it. It doesn’t replace the wiki.</PlainSummary>
    </div>
    <div class="emerge" aria-hidden="true"><Mark color="#EADFC6" /></div>
  </div>
</section>
